{"step_index":236,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:23:44Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Specificity**\n\nI'm focusing now on ensuring I choose the absolute best tool for each specific task. I am deliberately avoiding \"cat\" for file creation/appending, preferring dedicated commands. Also, I'm specifically aiming to avoid using \"grep\" within bash commands, favoring the `grep_search` command whenever appropriate. This commitment is intended to enhance precision and maintainability.\n\n\n**Analyzing Price Discrepancy**\n\nI've homed in on why the price shown might not be real-time. The `fetch_data` function's caching in `stock_screener.py`, with a 3600-second TTL, is the culprit! This means the data is cached for an hour. To fix this I can reduce the TTL, or remove the cache altogether for the freshest price.\n\n\n**Evaluating API Reliability**\n\nI'm now wrestling with the trade-offs of the caching strategy. Reducing the cache TTL, say to 60 or 300 seconds, offers fresher data but risks exacerbating Yahoo Finance's rate-limiting issues on the Streamlit Cloud server. My focus now is on balancing data freshness with the stability of the API calls, considering the potential for IP bans. I need to consider what the rate limit policy is.\n\n\n**Addressing Data Freshness**\n\nI've decided to address the user directly about the data freshness issue with Yahoo Finance and the rate limiting risk. Specifically, I plan to explain the 15-minute delay for some markets and the current 1-hour caching strategy designed to avoid an IP ban. I'll offer a 5-minute cache TTL as an improvement. To implement this, I'll modify the `fetch_data` function, changing the `ttl` to 300 seconds. While I considered `time.sleep`, I'm prioritizing the reduced TTL for now.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Reduce data caching from 1 hour to 5 minutes to provide more real-time prices.","EndLine":44,"Instruction":"Change ttl to 300 in fetch_data.","ReplacementContent":"@st.cache_data(ttl=300, show_spinner=False)\ndef fetch_data(ticker):","StartLine":43,"TargetContent":"@st.cache_data(ttl=3600, show_spinner=False)\ndef fetch_data(ticker):","TargetFile":"C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/stock_screener.py","TargetLintErrorIds":[],"toolAction":"Reducing cache time","toolSummary":"Reduce cache ttl"}}]}
