{"step_index":240,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:24:10Z","content":"There are two reasons why the prices you are seeing aren't strictly real-time:\n\n1. **App Caching (Just Fixed!):** To prevent your app from completely freezing or getting permanently IP-banned by Yahoo Finance, I originally set the app to \"remember\" prices for 1 hour. This meant the prices were delayed by up to 60 minutes! I have **just pushed an update to GitHub to reduce this memory to 5 minutes**, so your prices will now be much fresher!\n2. **Yahoo Finance Limits:** Because we are using a free data source (Yahoo Finance API), they naturally delay stock market data by about 15-20 minutes for Malaysian (Bursa) and some US stocks. \n\n### Why you are seeing so many yellow boxes\nIn your screenshot, you can see a bunch of yellow warnings saying `\"Yahoo Finance might be blocking the Cloud server\"`. \n\nBecause you are using the \"Discovery Scanner\" to scan 30 stocks back-to-back at lightning speed, Yahoo Finance's security systems detect it, assume you are a scraping bot, and temporarily cut off the data feed for the rest of the stocks on the list.\n\n**The Trade-off:**\nBy reducing the cache to 5 minutes (so you get fresher prices), the app will have to ask Yahoo for data more often, which unfortunately might result in seeing *more* of those yellow blocks when running the massive 30-stock scanner on Streamlit Cloud. \n\nWait 1-2 minutes for the Streamlit Cloud server to grab the latest GitHub code, and you should start seeing much more accurate prices!","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Specificity**\n\nI'm focusing intently on tool specificity. I've been refining my approach to avoid unnecessary use of bash commands for file creation or appending, opting for dedicated tools like `>` and `>>` respectively. I am also working to use `grep_search` more for searching, rather than general grep commands. I must remember to use the more efficient tools.\n\n\n"}
